Golden fixtures and runner for Prosper's remote frames protocol 1.0, copied
verbatim from ventsislav-georgiev/prosper 96b65ad (docs/protocol/golden/).
The spec is docs/protocol/remote-frames.md there. Do not edit these files:
re-copy them from a newer Prosper commit and update the commit named here.

Fixtures 17 and up are dch's own (#114), in the same format: the "ctl" op of
remote frames 1.1 (0x30 request; 0x31 stdout, 0x32 stderr, 0x33 exit). They
need "ctl" in ops. Two keys are dch's: "dch_serve" ({"args", "env"}) names
how the server must start (create off, a lowered cap, a lowered timeout);
those fixtures require the op "dch-serve-config", which no server names, so
a plain run.py run skips them. "dch_mirror" marks a fixture for the full
build only (--read, --keys and --follow need the terminal mirror).

tests/serve_test.py runs them against `dch serve` with --mutating, each
"dch_serve" group against a dch serve of its own.
